# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide explains how to use the [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") to implement quantum algorithms directly in fermionic space, rather than mapping to qubits first.\n"
msgstr "Panduan ini menjelaskan cara memakai [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") untuk menjalankan algoritma kuantum langsung di ruang fermionik, tanpa harus memetakannya ke qubit dulu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why use fermionic circuits {#why-use-fermionic-circuits}"
msgstr "Kenapa pakai circuit fermionik {#why-use-fermionic-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Consider the traditional workflow for implementing the time evolution of a fermionic Hamiltonian on a qubit-based architecture:\n"
msgstr "Coba lihat alur kerja tradisional untuk mengimplementasikan evolusi waktu dari Hamiltonian fermionik di arsitektur berbasis qubit:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '1.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define the fermionic Hamiltonian (for example, $H = \\sum_{pq} h_{pq} c^\\dagger_p c_q$).\n"
msgstr "Definisikan Hamiltonian fermionik (misalnya, $H = \\sum_{pq} h_{pq} c^\\dagger_p c_q$).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Map it to a qubit operator (for example, by using the Jordan-Wigner mapping).\n"
msgstr "Petakan ke operator qubit (misalnya, dengan pemetaan Jordan-Wigner).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '3.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Implement the time evolution in qubit space (using Trotterization or other methods).\n"
msgstr "Implementasikan evolusi waktu di ruang qubit (dengan Trotterization atau metode lain).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This approach has a fundamental limitation; early mapping to qubits discards problem-aware knowledge about the fermionic structure. Standard optimization passes cannot exploit fermionic symmetries or allowed term reorderings, resulting in suboptimal circuits with unnecessary depths and gate counts.\n"
msgstr "Pendekatan ini punya keterbatasan mendasar: pemetaan ke qubit di awal membuang pengetahuan yang sadar-masalah tentang struktur fermionik. Pass optimisasi standar tidak bisa memanfaatkan simetri fermionik atau penataan ulang suku yang diperbolehkan, sehingga circuit yang dihasilkan kurang optimal dengan depth dan jumlah gate yang tidak perlu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") enables a better workflow:\n"
msgstr "[`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") memungkinkan alur kerja yang lebih baik:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Implement the time evolution directly in fermionic space using fermionic gates.\n"
msgstr "Implementasikan evolusi waktu langsung di ruang fermionik dengan gate fermionik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '3.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Map to qubit space as part of the transpilation process.\n"
msgstr "Petakan ke ruang qubit sebagai bagian dari proses transpilasi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This approach addresses the limitation by keeping problem-aware knowledge in fermionic space, where optimization passes can exploit fermionic structure and commutation relations to reduce circuit depth. The fermionic circuit describes what computation to perform, while transpilation handles how to map it to qubits, providing a cleaner separation of concerns.\n"
msgstr "Pendekatan ini mengatasi keterbatasan tadi dengan menjaga pengetahuan yang sadar-masalah tetap di ruang fermionik, tempat pass optimisasi bisa memanfaatkan struktur fermionik dan relasi komutasi untuk memangkas depth circuit. Circuit fermionik menjelaskan komputasi apa yang dilakukan, sedangkan transpilasi menangani cara memetakannya ke qubit, sehingga pemisahan tanggung jawabnya lebih bersih.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generic mode indexing {#generic-mode-indexing}"
msgstr "Pengindeksan mode generik {#generic-mode-indexing}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both the [`operators`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators#module-qiskit_fermions.operators \"qiskit_fermions.operators\") module and the [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") use generic mode-based indexing that makes no assumptions about the nature of the modes. A mode is simply an abstract index labeling a fermionic degree of freedom, with no inherent semantics. This design choice mirrors the operators module and ensures maximum flexibility. For example, you can implement time evolution for any operator implementing the [`OperatorTrait`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait\") protocol, regardless of its mathematical representation.\n"
msgstr "Baik modul [`operators`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators#module-qiskit_fermions.operators \"qiskit_fermions.operators\") maupun [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") memakai pengindeksan berbasis mode yang generik dan tidak berasumsi apa pun soal sifat modenya. Mode hanyalah indeks abstrak yang memberi label pada satu derajat kebebasan fermionik, tanpa semantik bawaan. Pilihan desain ini meniru modul operators dan memastikan fleksibilitas maksimum. Misalnya, kamu bisa mengimplementasikan evolusi waktu untuk operator apa pun yang mengimplementasikan protokol [`OperatorTrait`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait\"), apa pun representasi matematisnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build a fermionic circuit {#build-a-fermionic-circuit}"
msgstr "Membangun circuit fermionik {#build-a-fermionic-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The example below implements the time evolution described in the previous section. It constructs a [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") by specifying the number of fermionic modes, then adds fermionic gates from the [`qiskit_fermions.circuit.library`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library#module-qiskit_fermions.circuit.library \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library\") to implement the time evolution.\n"
msgstr "Contoh di bawah ini mengimplementasikan evolusi waktu yang dijelaskan di bagian sebelumnya. Contoh ini membuat [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") dengan menentukan jumlah mode fermionik, lalu menambahkan gate fermionik dari [`qiskit_fermions.circuit.library`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library#module-qiskit_fermions.circuit.library \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library\") untuk mengimplementasikan evolusi waktu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The example also demonstrates how to incorporate domain knowledge into an operator by using [operator term grouping](grouping#grouping-explanation). By assigning group indices to the Hamiltonian terms, you preserve structural information that optimization passes can exploit throughout the transpilation stack.\n"
msgstr "Contoh ini juga menunjukkan cara memasukkan pengetahuan domain ke dalam operator dengan [pengelompokan suku operator](grouping#grouping-explanation). Dengan memberi indeks grup pada suku-suku Hamiltonian, kamu mempertahankan informasi struktural yang bisa dimanfaatkan pass optimisasi di seluruh stack transpilasi.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A simple \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with a single time evolution gate.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-2.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A simple \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with a single time evolution gate.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-2.avif)\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A decomposed \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with several time evolution gates.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-3.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A decomposed \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with several time evolution gates.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-3.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Notice how the operator term grouping is preserved even in simple operations like decomposition. This demonstrates how structural information flows through the circuit stack. To understand the full transpilation to qubits, refer to the [Transpiling fermionic circuits](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) guide.\n"
msgstr "Perhatikan bahwa pengelompokan suku operator tetap terjaga bahkan pada operasi sederhana seperti dekomposisi. Ini menunjukkan bagaimana informasi struktural mengalir melalui stack circuit. Untuk memahami transpilasi lengkap ke qubit, lihat panduan [Transpiling fermionic circuits](transpilation#transpilation-explanation).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keep gates apart with a barrier {#keep-gates-apart-with-a-barrier}"
msgstr "Pisahkan gate dengan barrier {#keep-gates-apart-with-a-barrier}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The optimization passes fuse neighboring gates where they can. For example, [`MergeOrbitalRotations`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-orbital-rotations#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations\") combines a run of consecutive [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") gates into one, and [`MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-slater-determinant-preparation#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation\") folds an [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") into the rotation that follows it.\n"
msgstr "Pass optimisasi menggabungkan gate bertetangga kalau bisa. Misalnya, [`MergeOrbitalRotations`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-orbital-rotations#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations\") menggabungkan rangkaian gate [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") yang berurutan menjadi satu, dan [`MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-slater-determinant-preparation#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation\") melipat [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") ke dalam rotasi yang mengikutinya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use [`FermionicCircuit.barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier\") when you want to prevent that. A barrier carries no unitary effect, so it does not change the state your circuit prepares; it only marks a point that the passes do not fuse across. Call it without arguments to span every mode, or pass the modes to restrict it to:\n"
msgstr "Pakai [`FermionicCircuit.barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier\") kalau kamu ingin mencegah hal itu. Barrier tidak punya efek uniter, jadi tidak mengubah state yang disiapkan circuit-mu; barrier hanya menandai titik yang tidak dilewati penggabungan oleh pass. Panggil tanpa argumen untuk mencakup semua mode, atau berikan mode-mode yang ingin dibatasi:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with a barrier separating two orbital rotations.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-5.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with a barrier separating two orbital rotations.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-5.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Barriers survive the fermion-to-qubit transpilation, so they also constrain the qubit-level optimization that follows. The [Transpile fermionic circuits](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) guide covers that stage.\n"
msgstr "Barrier tetap bertahan setelah transpilasi fermion-ke-qubit, jadi barrier juga membatasi optimisasi tingkat qubit yang menyusul. Panduan [Transpile fermionic circuits](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) membahas tahap itu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Repeat a circuit {#repeat-a-circuit}"
msgstr "Mengulang circuit {#repeat-a-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Many algorithms apply the same block of gates many times over. Time evolution is the common case: a Trotter step is built once, then repeated to reach the target time. Use [`repeat()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.repeat \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.repeat\") to build the repeated circuit, and [`compose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.compose \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.compose\") to join it to a state preparation prefix.\n"
msgstr "Banyak algoritma menerapkan blok gate yang sama berkali-kali. Evolusi waktu adalah kasus yang paling umum: satu langkah Trotter dibuat sekali, lalu diulang sampai mencapai waktu target. Pakai [`repeat()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.repeat \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.repeat\") untuk membuat circuit berulang, dan [`compose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.compose \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.compose\") untuk menyambungkannya ke prefiks persiapan state.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The example below builds a second-order Trotter step for a Fermi-Hubbard model. The step is symmetric: it splits the hopping term into two half-duration [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") gates surrounding the on-site interaction.\n"
msgstr "Contoh di bawah ini membuat langkah Trotter orde kedua untuk model Fermi-Hubbard. Langkahnya simetris: suku hopping dipecah menjadi dua gate [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") berdurasi setengah yang mengapit interaksi on-site.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Repeating the step and composing it onto a Hartree-Fock reference gives the full evolution:\n"
msgstr "Mengulang langkah itu dan menyusunnya di atas referensi Hartree-Fock menghasilkan evolusi penuh:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with repeated steps.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-8.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with repeated steps.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-8.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The repetitions are flattened into the returned circuit rather than wrapped in a single gate, so [`count_ops()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.count_ops \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.count_ops\") counts two rotations per step. That flattening is what makes the redundancy at the step boundaries visible to the transpiler: the trailing half-duration rotation of one step and the leading one of the next are adjacent, so [`MergeOrbitalRotations`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-orbital-rotations#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations\") combines them into a single rotation.\n"
msgstr "Pengulangan diratakan ke dalam circuit yang dikembalikan, bukan dibungkus dalam satu gate, sehingga [`count_ops()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.count_ops \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.count_ops\") menghitung dua rotasi per langkah. Perataan itulah yang membuat redundansi di batas antarlangkah terlihat oleh transpiler: rotasi berdurasi setengah di akhir satu langkah dan yang di awal langkah berikutnya saling bersebelahan, sehingga [`MergeOrbitalRotations`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-orbital-rotations#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations\") menggabungkannya menjadi satu rotasi.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with repeated steps and merged orbital rotations.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-10.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with repeated steps and merged orbital rotations.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-10.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The result costs one rotation per step plus one, which is what you get by fusing those half-steps by hand. Writing the step in its natural symmetric form and repeating it produces the same circuit, so the fusion is left to the optimization stage.\n"
msgstr "Hasilnya membutuhkan satu rotasi per langkah ditambah satu, sama seperti kalau kamu menggabungkan setengah-langkah itu secara manual. Menulis langkah dalam bentuk simetris alaminya lalu mengulangnya menghasilkan circuit yang sama, jadi penggabungannya diserahkan ke tahap optimisasi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When you need the repetitions kept apart, pass `insert_barriers=True` to place a [`barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier\") between them. The optimization passes do not fuse gates across a barrier, so every rotation survives:\n"
msgstr "Kalau kamu perlu pengulangan tetap terpisah, berikan `insert_barriers=True` untuk menempatkan [`barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier\") di antaranya. Pass optimisasi tidak menggabungkan gate melintasi barrier, sehingga setiap rotasi tetap ada:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with repeated steps separated by barriers.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-12.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with repeated steps separated by barriers.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-12.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The `reps` argument of [`FermionicSuzukiTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-suzuki-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter\") is a different concept. It subdivides a single [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate into more, shorter factors, whereas [`repeat()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.repeat \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.repeat\") duplicates whole circuits. Repeating a circuit that holds one [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") only multiplies its total evolution time.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Catatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Argumen `reps` dari [`FermionicSuzukiTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-suzuki-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter\") adalah konsep yang berbeda. Argumen itu membagi satu gate [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") menjadi lebih banyak faktor yang lebih pendek, sedangkan [`repeat()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.repeat \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.repeat\") menggandakan seluruh circuit. Mengulang circuit yang berisi satu [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") hanya melipatgandakan total waktu evolusinya.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measure fermionic modes {#measure-fermionic-modes}"
msgstr "Mengukur mode fermionik {#measure-fermionic-modes}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`measure_all()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure_all \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure_all\") reads every mode out into a classical bit of its own, pairing mode `i` with bit `i`. Use [`measure()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure\") with your own [`ClassicalRegister`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/circuit#qiskit.circuit.ClassicalRegister) to read out only some of them.\n"
msgstr "[`measure_all()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure_all \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure_all\") membaca setiap mode ke bit klasiknya sendiri, dengan memasangkan mode `i` dengan bit `i`. Pakai [`measure()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure\") dengan [`ClassicalRegister`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/circuit#qiskit.circuit.ClassicalRegister) milikmu sendiri untuk membaca sebagian mode saja.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Passing `inplace=False` returns a measured copy and leaves the original alone, which matters because a measurement is not unitary: a circuit carrying one can no longer be applied to a state vector, so keep an unmeasured circuit around if you also want to simulate it.\n"
msgstr "Memberikan `inplace=False` mengembalikan salinan yang sudah diukur dan membiarkan aslinya tidak berubah. Ini penting karena pengukuran tidak uniter: circuit yang memuat pengukuran tidak bisa lagi diterapkan ke state vector, jadi simpan circuit tanpa pengukuran kalau kamu juga ingin mensimulasikannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measuring here, rather than on the transpiled [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit), is what keeps the sampled bitstrings easy to read. A fermionic measurement names the mode it reads, so every stage that moves modes around ([`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\") at the fermionic level, layout and routing at the qubit level) carries the measurement along with it, and the bitstring stays indexed by the mode you asked about.\n"
msgstr "Mengukur di sini, bukan pada [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit) hasil transpilasi, membuat bitstring hasil sampling tetap mudah dibaca. Pengukuran fermionik menyebut mode yang dibacanya, sehingga setiap tahap yang memindahkan mode ([`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\") di tingkat fermionik, layout dan routing di tingkat qubit) ikut membawa pengukurannya, dan bitstring tetap diindeks menurut mode yang kamu tanyakan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Unlike [`measure_all()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#measure_all), no [`barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier\") is inserted before the measurements. Call [`barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier\") yourself first if you want one there.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Catatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Berbeda dengan [`measure_all()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#measure_all), tidak ada [`barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier\") yang disisipkan sebelum pengukuran. Panggil [`barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier\") sendiri lebih dulu kalau kamu menginginkannya di situ.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Whether a measured bit means what you expect depends on the fermion-to-qubit encoding, which is chosen during transpilation rather than here. Under an occupation-basis encoding such as Jordan-Wigner each mode is carried by one qubit and the bit is that mode’s occupation; see [`FermionicMeasure`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-fermionic-measure#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.FermionicMeasure \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.FermionicMeasure\").\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Apakah bit hasil ukur bermakna seperti yang kamu harapkan tergantung pada encoding fermion-ke-qubit, yang dipilih saat transpilasi, bukan di sini. Pada encoding basis okupasi seperti Jordan-Wigner, setiap mode dibawa oleh satu qubit dan bitnya adalah okupasi mode tersebut; lihat [`FermionicMeasure`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-fermionic-measure#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.FermionicMeasure \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.FermionicMeasure\").\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpile fermionic circuits {#transpile-fermionic-circuits}"
msgstr "Transpilasi circuit fermionik {#transpile-fermionic-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To implement the quantum algorithm represented by your [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") it must be transpiled to a [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit). You can learn how to do this in the [Transpile fermionic circuits](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) guide.\n"
msgstr "Untuk mengimplementasikan algoritma kuantum yang diwakili oleh [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") milikmu, circuit itu harus ditranspilasi menjadi [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit). Cara melakukannya ada di panduan [Transpile fermionic circuits](transpilation#transpilation-explanation).\n"

